# Repositories

## Base class

All repositories extend `App\Repositories\Repository` and pass the model class to `parent::__construct()`:

```php
class QuestionRepository extends Repository
{
    public function __construct()
    {
        parent::__construct(Question::class);
    }
}
```

Namespace: `App\Repositories\v1\` or `App\Repositories\v1\{Domain}\` (e.g. `Comment\CommentRepository`).

## Writes (use base methods)

| Operation | Method |
|-----------|--------|
| Single save | `save(Model $model)` |
| Insert rows | `insert(array $data)` |
| Single/bulk delete | `delete()`, `bulkDelete()`, `bulkForceDelete()` |
| Bulk update | `bulkUpdate(array $ids, array $attributes)` |

Base methods throw `App\Exceptions\v1\RepositoryException` on failure. Services catch and handle; repositories do not swallow errors silently.

## Reads and domain queries

Put **entity-specific query logic** in the repository, not in services:

```php
// StatisticsRepository — good
public function findByUserAndQuestion(int $userId, int $questionId): ?Statistic
{
    return Statistic::query()
        ->byUserAndQuestion($userId, $questionId)
        ->first();
}

public function createNotMet(int $userId, int $questionId): void
{
    $statistic = new Statistic();
    // set attributes…
    $this->save($statistic);
}
```

Prefer model scopes (`->byUserAndQuestion()`) inside repository methods. Add new finder/counter/create helpers here when a query is reused or non-trivial.

## Do not

- Call `$model->save()` from services — use `$repository->save($model)`
- Duplicate the same `Model::query()` chain across multiple services
- Put Filament- or HTTP-specific logic in repositories
